# Dev Notes 46 — Runtime Model-Bundle Route Validation v1

**Date:** 2026-06-18  
**Branch:** `runtime-model-bundle-route-validation-v1`  
**Status:** Merged to `main` and main-inspected for the declared contract-only scope; assistant sandbox syntax checks, targeted model-bundle route-validation smoke, existing contract-chain smokes, fixture helper check, worker import-cycle check, public-entrypoint guard, artifact guard, package extraction/recheck, Michael-run local Windows/MINGW64 candidate checks, direct GitHub branch inspection, and direct GitHub `main` inspection passed. No real-runtime test required for the declared contract-only scope because this branch does not touch runtime/worker/lifecycle/native execution surfaces.

---

## 1. Purpose

This branch adds a narrow, contract-only route validation seam that checks whether a selected capability route can legally pair with declared model bundle and hardware profile metadata.

The branch fills the gap left after:

```text
runtime-model-bundle-registry-v1
runtime-hardware-profile-registry-v1
```

Those branches created static registries and lookup helpers. They intentionally did not validate cross-registry existence or compatibility. This branch adds the cross-registry compatibility seam without executing backends or changing runtime behavior.

---

## 2. Scope

In scope:

```text
route-selected modelBundleId existence checks
route-selected or bundle-default hardwareProfileId existence checks
selectable model bundle and hardware profile status checks
route capability vs model bundle capability compatibility
route capability vs hardware profile capability compatibility
route backendKind vs model bundle backendKind compatibility
route backendKind vs hardware profile backendKinds compatibility
route/backend bundle backendId agreement when both are declared
metadata-only future vision route validation without execution
```

Out of scope:

```text
model loading
filesystem model/projector path checks
image/video execution
llama-mtmd-cli execution
llama-server execution
workerBridge calls
runtime.mjs public API changes
configOverride expansion
runtime hardware probing
native/model execution
Capability Bus executor integration
memory/storage backend work
Cognitive Graph Runtime work
cleanup or optimization outside the declared files
```

---

