## 5. Implementation summary

Added `runtime/router/capabilityRouteModelBundlePlan.mjs` as the modular route/model/profile compatibility helper.

New contract version:

```js
CAPABILITY_ROUTE_MODEL_BUNDLE_PLAN_CONTRACT_VERSION = "capability-route-model-bundle-plan.v1"
```

New public router contract exports:

```js
validateCapabilityRouteModelBundlePlan(routePlan, {
    modelBundleRegistry,
    hardwareProfileRegistry
});

assertCapabilityRouteModelBundlePlan(routePlan, registries);
normalizeCapabilityRouteModelBundlePlan(routePlan, registries);
```

Accepted result shape:

```js
{
    contractVersion: "capability-route-model-bundle-plan.v1",
    routePlan,
    modelBundle,
    hardwareProfile,
    effectiveHardwareProfileId
}
```

The helper treats `routePlan` as the output of the existing route-plan contract. It validates the plan descriptor shape, then performs only metadata compatibility checks.

---

## 6. Validation rules added

Model bundle checks when `route.modelBundleId` is present:

```text
modelBundleRegistry is required
bundle must exist
bundle status must be selectable
route capability must be included in bundle.capabilities
route backendKind must match bundle.backendKind
route backendId and bundle.backendId must match when both are declared
```

Hardware profile checks when an effective profile ID exists:

```text
effectiveHardwareProfileId = route.hardwareProfileId ?? modelBundle.defaultHardwareProfileId
hardwareProfileRegistry is required
profile must exist
profile status must be selectable
route capability must be included in profile.capabilities
route backendKind must be included in profile.backendKinds
```

If a route has no model bundle ID and no effective hardware profile ID, the helper does not invent one and does not require registries. Existing route/service/backend validators continue to own required-presence checks.

---

## 7. Architecture boundaries preserved

```text
Model Bundle Registry remains metadata-only.
Hardware Profile Registry remains metadata-only.
Capability Router remains a planning/validation surface.
Backend adapters are not executed.
No model files are loaded or checked.
No runtime hardware probing is performed.
No public API shape changes.
No worker/native/model execution surfaces are touched.
```

Future vision metadata is allowed as metadata only. The smoke test confirms a `vision.chat` route can validate against a `gguf-mmproj` model bundle and a CLI-shaped hardware profile without executing any media backend.

